\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Behold Me standing at the door,
\par And hear Me pleading evermore,
\par With gentle voice: O heart of sin,
\par May I come in? May I come in?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Behold Me standing at the door,
\par And hear Me pleading evermore:
\par Say, weary heart, oppressed with sin,
\par May I come in? May I come in?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I bore the cruel thorns for thee,
\par I waited long and patiently:
\par Say, weary heart, oppressed with sin,
\par May I come in? May I come in?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Behold Me standing at the door,
\par And hear Me pleading evermore:
\par Say, weary heart, oppressed with sin,
\par May I come in? May I come in?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I would not plead with thee in vain;
\par Remember all My grief and pain!
\par I died to ransom thee from sin,
\par May I come in? May I come in?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Behold Me standing at the door,
\par And hear Me pleading evermore:
\par Say, weary heart, oppressed with sin,
\par May I come in? May I come in?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I bring thee joy from heaven above,
\par I bring thee pardon, peace, and love:
\par Say, weary heart, oppressed with sin,
\par May I come in? May I come in?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Behold Me standing at the door,
\par And hear Me pleading evermore:
\par Say, weary heart, oppressed with sin,
\par May I come in? May I come in?
\par \f1 
